      "attribution": "Executed classification: the cloaking comes from the version gate of Go b4e7dbd2 (fix(claude): bump Claude Code CLI fingerprint baseline to 2.1.321, C1 #69 scope), not from C2's detection commits. Its parent 19a0a854 already contains 20c9095c, 6d4102f3 and 542a525f and forwards callers 2.1.280, 2.1.290, 2.1.320, 2.1.321 and 2.1.322 natively and cloaks 2.1.279. b4e7dbd2 and 8bba7a77 cloak 2.1.279 through 2.1.320 and forward 2.1.321 and 2.1.322. v8.0.35 (ae3ee3be) forwards 2.1.280 and later. The variants differ from native-signals only in the caller's User-Agent version. This classifies observed Go behaviour only: whether cloaking a genuine 2.1.280 client is correct on the wire stays unknown until C2 records client provenance, the entry grants no adoption, and moving it to #69 is a tracker decision (harness/evidence/attribution-20261112.json.gz)."
