    "credential-disabled-persist": {
      "kind": "unowned",
      "issue": "https://github.com/zakstak/cliproxy-rs/issues/66",
      "evidence": "Executed first-parent bisect between 8a01bc02 (persists disabled: false) and 4f2e5270 (field absent): the first change is Go 091ff27f (feat(antigravity): persist model capability hints in auth metadata, which reworks shared auth persistence in sdk/cliproxy/auth/conductor_persistence.go and persist_policy.go). Its parent a2718314 persists disabled: false and 091ff27f leaves the field absent, in 3 of 3 runs each. 091ff27f is in v8.0.35: executed v8.0.35 (ae3ee3be) already leaves disabled absent, so cliproxy-rs differs from the frozen default reference here too, which no ledger entry records yet. No tracker issue owns it (harness/evidence/attribution-20261112.json.gz)."
    },
    "error-retry-after": {
      "kind": "unowned",
      "issue": "https://github.com/zakstak/cliproxy-rs/issues/66",
      "evidence": "Executed pair: Go 9a35fa12 (fix(codex): treat turn_rate_limit_exceeded as transient capacity with retry hint, which adds trustedRetryAfterError and HasTrustedRetryDeadline) answers all six cases with its own whole-second Retry-After; its parent c3767123 and v8.0.35 (ae3ee3be) send none, as cliproxy-rs and v8.0.10 do. The writer at sdk/api/handlers/handlers_errors.go:127-128 predates v8.0.10; the trusted local deadline it now writes is new. N1 #111 references the commit for Codex; no tracker issue owns the Claude-visible effect (harness/evidence/attribution-20261112.json.gz)."
    },
